<title>IRAN: OPEC compliance committee to meet May 7.</title>
<headline>OPEC compliance committee to meet May 7.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC's ministerial output monitoring committee will meet in the Iranian city of Isfahan on May 7 to discuss the 11-member group's quota compliance, OPEC delegate sources in Iran said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Independent assessments of OPEC production estimate that the organisation is producing close to 27 million barrels per day (bpd), above its agreed supply ceiling of 25.03 million bpd.</p>
<p>The monitoring committee is currently chaired by Iran's Oil Minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh and comprises Indonesia's Ida Bagus Sudjana and Nigerian oil minister Dan Etete.</p>
<p>Venezuela's Energy and Mines minister Erwin Arrieta will also attend the meeting, the Venezuelan Energy and Mines Ministry said in a statement on Monday.</p>
</text>
